-- READS-DIFFERENTLY-ON-MAIN: 6 of 68 traces class differently on the stable binary (main) from the unstable one (the EXPECT above each is the unstable class).
-- The cause in every case is one: main ignores a LEST after a MAY, so a MAY that lapses (or whose act comes too late) ends FULFILLED on main, where the unstable binary moves on to the LEST's next step and leaves the plaintiff's route open.
-- Five more traces match on main for a different reason: they come after a lapse (the court approves on day 220, on day 120; the court is not convinced after a lapse, twice; and the 75-day step's gate-fails trace), and main is already FULFILLED at the lapse and never reaches the court step or its gate.
-- line 221: unstable RESIDUAL, main FULFILLED: 197(3): decided to file; notice on day 20; filing on day 96 is late, so the plaintiff's route opens.
-- line 229: unstable RESIDUAL, main FULFILLED: 197(3): decided to file; notice on day 20; no filing by day 200: the plaintiff's route is open.
-- line 237: unstable RESIDUAL, main FULFILLED: 197(3): decided to file, no filing; the plaintiff asks the court on day 210; the court must decide.
-- line 299: unstable RESIDUAL, main FULFILLED: 197(3): the seventy-sixth day is late: the plaintiff's route opens.
-- line 311: unstable RESIDUAL, main FULFILLED: 197(3): no filing by day 200: the plaintiff's route is open.
-- line 317: unstable RESIDUAL, main FULFILLED: 197(3), 198(א): no filing; the plaintiff asks on day 100; the court must decide.
